separate linguistic domains.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A004\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\n    \"stem\": \"The connotation of 'childlike' compared with 'youthful' is…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"More positive\",\n      \"More negative\",\n      \"Identical\",\n      \"Ambiguous\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"'Childlike' can suggest immaturity, while 'youthful' is more positive.\",\n      \"Correct! 'Childlike' often carries negative connotations of immaturity compared to the positive 'youthful.'\",\n      \"The words have different emotional associations.\",\n      \"The distinction is clear in most contexts.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 3\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A005\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Meaning & Communication\",\n    \"stem\": \"Which rhetorical appeal relies on credibility?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Logos\",\n      \"Pathos\",\n      \"Ethos\",\n      \"Kairos\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Logos appeals to logic and reason.\",\n      \"Pathos appeals to emotions.\",\n      \"Correct! Ethos establishes speaker credibility and trustworthiness.\",\n      \"Kairos refers to opportune timing in rhetoric.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A006\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\n    \"stem\": \"In poetry, a caesura refers to…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"A pause within a line\",\n      \"End rhyme\",\n      \"A stanza break\",\n      \"A change in theme\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! A caesura is a deliberate pause or break within a poetic line.\",\n      \"End rhyme occurs at line endings, not within lines.\",\n      \"Stanza breaks separate groups of lines.\",\n      \"Thematic shifts are conceptual, not structural pauses.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 3\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A007\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\n    \"stem\": \"The main function of an unreliable narrator is to…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Simplify plot structure\",\n      \"Create irony and reader skepticism\",\n      \"Clarify moral lessons\",\n      \"Provide historical accuracy\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Unreliable narrators often complicate, not simplify, plot.\",\n      \"Correct! Unreliable narrators create dramatic irony as readers question the truth of the narrative.\",\n      \"Unreliable narrators obscure rather than clarify morals.\",\n      \"Historical accuracy is compromised by unreliable narration.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 3\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A008\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\n    \"stem\": \"In a Shakespearean sonnet, the volta usually occurs…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"After line 4\",\n      \"After line 8 or 9\",\n      \"In the closing couplet only\",\n      \"At the midpoint of line 7\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Line 4 is too early; that's after the first quatrain.\",\n      \"Correct! The volta (turn) typically occurs at line 9 or in the final couplet.\",\n      \"While the couplet can contain a turn, line 9 is more common.\",\n      \"Line 7 is not a traditional volta position.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 3\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A009\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\n    \"stem\": \"A recurring image of water symbolizing rebirth is an example of…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Allusion\",\n      \"Motif\",\n      \"Conflict\",\n      \"Foreshadowing\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Allusion references other works or events.\",\n      \"Correct! A motif is a recurring symbol or image that reinforces theme.\",\n      \"Conflict is the struggle between opposing forces.\",\n      \"Foreshadowing hints at future events.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A010\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Literature & Understanding\",\n    \"stem\": \"Which statement best defines theme?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"The sequence of events in a story\",\n      \"The setting and atmosphere\",\n      \"The central idea or insight about life\",\n      \"The author's writing style\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Sequence of events describes plot.\",\n      \"Setting provides context, not theme.\",\n      \"Correct! Theme is the underlying message or universal truth.\",\n      \"Writing style relates to voice and technique.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A011\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\n    \"stem\": \"Diction refers to an author's…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Word choice\",\n      \"Sentence length\",\n      \"Tone\",\n      \"Figurative imagery\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Diction is the selection and use of specific words.\",\n      \"Sentence length relates to syntax.\",\n      \"Tone is created through diction but isn't diction itself.\",\n      \"Imagery is descriptive language, not word choice per se.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A012\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\n    \"stem\": \"A narrative that begins in medias res starts…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"At the very beginning of events\",\n      \"In the middle of the action\",\n      \"With background exposition only\",\n      \"After the resolution\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"In medias res means 'in the middle of things.'\",\n      \"Correct! In medias res begins amid action, then fills in backstory.\",\n      \"Background exposition is avoided in in medias res openings.\",\n      \"Starting after resolution would be unusual.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A013\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\n    \"stem\": \"The use of short, choppy sentences most directly affects…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Rhythm and pacing\",\n      \"Imagery and tone\",\n      \"Theme development\",\n      \"Symbolic meaning\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Short sentences create quick rhythm and fast pacing.\",\n      \"While they can affect tone, rhythm is the primary effect.\",\n      \"Theme is developed through content, not sentence length.\",\n      \"Symbolism uses objects and images, not syntax.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A014\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\n    \"stem\": \"When a writer varies sentence structure for emphasis, they are manipulating…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Syntax\",\n      \"Diction\",\n      \"Theme\",\n      \"Motif\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Syntax is the arrangement of words and sentence structure.\",\n      \"Diction is word choice, not sentence structure.\",\n      \"Theme is conceptual content.\",\n      \"Motif is a recurring element.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A015\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Genre & Craft\",\n    \"stem\": \"Which genre feature most clearly distinguishes drama from prose fiction?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Dialogue and stage directions\",\n      \"Internal monologue\",\n      \"Narrative exposition\",\n      \"Figurative language\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 0,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Correct! Drama relies on dialogue and stage directions rather than narrative prose.\",\n      \"Internal monologue is typical of prose fiction, not drama.\",\n      \"Drama minimizes narrative exposition.\",\n      \"Both genres use figurative language.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A016\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\n    \"stem\": \"Formative assessment is used primarily to…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Rank students for grading\",\n      \"Adjust instruction during learning\",\n      \"Certify end-of-unit mastery\",\n      \"Measure statewide performance\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Ranking is not the primary purpose of formative assessment.\",\n      \"Correct! Formative assessment guides ongoing instructional decisions.\",\n      \"End-of-unit mastery is measured by summative assessment.\",\n      \"Statewide measures are standardized summative assessments.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A017\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\n    \"stem\": \"In reading instruction, fluency involves…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Memorization\",\n      \"Speed only\",\n      \"Accuracy, rate, and expression\",\n      \"Vocabulary knowledge\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 2,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Fluency is automatic decoding, not memorization.\",\n      \"Speed is one component but not sufficient alone.\",\n      \"Correct! Fluency includes accuracy, appropriate rate, and prosody (expression).\",\n      \"Vocabulary supports comprehension but isn't fluency.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A018\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\n    \"stem\": \"The writing process stage focused on reorganizing ideas is…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Drafting\",\n      \"Revising\",\n      \"Editing\",\n      \"Publishing\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Drafting generates initial content.\",\n      \"Correct! Revising involves reorganizing, adding, and refining ideas.\",\n      \"Editing focuses on grammar and mechanics.\",\n      \"Publishing is the final sharing stage.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A019\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\n    \"stem\": \"Differentiated instruction means…\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Using one uniform method for equity\",\n      \"Varying methods to meet learner needs\",\n      \"Grouping by identical ability\",\n      \"Simplifying all content\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Uniform methods don't address diverse needs.\",\n      \"Correct! Differentiation tailors instruction to individual readiness, interests, and learning profiles.\",\n      \"Flexible grouping, not rigid ability grouping, is preferred.\",\n      \"Content rigor is maintained, not simplified.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A020\",\n    \"subarea\": \"Skills & Processes\",\n    \"stem\": \"Metacognitive readers do which of the following?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Read mechanically without reflection\",\n      \"Monitor and adjust comprehension strategies\",\n      \"Focus only on speed\",\n      \"Avoid annotation\"\n    ],\n    \"correctIndex\": 1,\n    \"rationales\": [\n      \"Metacognition requires active reflection, not mechanical reading.\",\n      \"Correct! Metacognitive readers think about their thinking and adjust strategies as needed.\",\n      \"Speed without monitoring comprehension isn't metacognitive.\",\n      \"Annotation is a metacognitive strategy.\"\n    ],\n    \"difficulty\": 3\n  }\n];\n});","lineCount":384,"map":[[384,3]],"functionMap":null},"type":"js/module"}]}